# Assignment 1 – TCP/IP Layers and Protocols

## Description

The TCP/IP model is the foundation of modern computer networking. It defines how data is transmitted between devices over a network.

---

## TCP/IP Layers

| Layer | Purpose |
|--------|---------|
| Application Layer | Provides network services to user applications. |
| Transport Layer | Ensures reliable communication using TCP or UDP. |
| Internet Layer | Handles IP addressing and routing. |
| Network Access Layer | Transmits data over the physical network. |

---

## Common Protocols and Port Numbers

| Protocol | Port | Purpose |
|----------|------|---------|
| FTP | 21 | File Transfer |
| SSH | 22 | Secure Remote Login |
| Telnet | 23 | Remote Login |
| SMTP | 25 | Email Transfer |
| DNS | 53 | Domain Name Resolution |
| DHCP | 67/68 | Dynamic IP Assignment |
| HTTP | 80 | Web Communication |
| POP3 | 110 | Email Retrieval |
| IMAP | 143 | Email Access |
| HTTPS | 443 | Secure Web Communication |
| SMB | 445 | File Sharing |
| RDP | 3389 | Remote Desktop |

