# Assignment 2 – Common HTTP Response Codes

## Description

HTTP response codes indicate the result of a client's request to a web server. They help developers and security professionals understand server responses during testing.

---

## Common Response Codes

| Code | Meaning |
|------|---------|
| 200 | OK |
| 201 | Created |
| 301 | Moved Permanently |
| 302 | Found (Temporary Redirect) |
| 400 | Bad Request |
| 401 | Unauthorized |
| 403 | Forbidden |
| 404 | Not Found |
| 500 | Internal Server Error |
| 503 | Service Unavailable |

---

## Learning Outcome

- Learned common HTTP status codes.
- Understood how API responses indicate success or failure.
